+
+## Highest-priority release actions
+
+1. Block payment dispatch until fraud screening is mandatory and fail-closed (F-01/F-09).
+2. Make scheme and ledger operations durable, idempotent and reconcilable across timeout/unknown outcomes (F-02/F-03/F-07/F-08/F-17).
+3. Stop treating the local balance copy as authoritative for money-critical decisions; add concurrency protection (F-04/F-05).
+4. Fix working-day/holiday calculation and monitor the 06:00 queue job (F-06).
+5. Implement or explicitly defer with an operational control the ledger-checked closure and month-end statement processes (F-13/F-14).
+6. Add production observability: dependency latency/error rates, payment state transitions, unknown/failed/overdue queues, reconciliation breaks, notification failures, access denials and SLOs (F-10/F-11/F-15/F-18).
+
+## Detection and review cadence
+
+At minimum, operations should review daily: `SUBMISSION_UNKNOWN`, `POSTING_FAILED`, queued payments past execution date, fraud holds older than four hours, ledger-versus-account balance differences, scheme settlement-versus-local payment differences, notification failures and duplicate-reference attempts. Finance should reconcile by payment reference at 07:00, and the FMEA scores should be revisited after the first production month and after every material payment, identity, ledger or scheme change.
